        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a8501484-9b63-5d8f-9ec2-1c8276cfec87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Il trovatore, La rondine, Rigoletto, Elena da Feltre, El trovador\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Giacomo Puccini, Giuseppe Adami, Alfred Maria Willner, Pietro Neri-Baraldi\n- Organizations: Teatro del Corso\n- Places: Bologna\n- Roles: Manrico, Duke of Mantua, Ubaldo\n\nFacts:\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play \"El trovador\".\n- Giuseppe Verdi's opera \"Il trovatore\" is an opera in four acts with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano and based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's 1836 play \"El trovador\".\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso.\n- By 1853 in Bologna, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang Manrico in the first performance there of \"Il trovatore\".\n- By 1853 in Bologna, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang the Duke of Mantua in the first performance there of \"Rigoletto\".\n- By 1853 in Bologna, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang Ubaldo in the first performance there of \"Elena da Feltre\".\n- Giacomo Puccini's opera \"La rondine\" is an opera in three acts with an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner and another author not named in the chunk.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8d930507-04cc-572f-8226-c64da5ada461",
